          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            In
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classical+mathematics"} classical mathematics
            %em countable
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ordinal"} ordinal
            is the
            %span.newWikiWord
              order type
              %a{:href => "/nlab/new/order+type"} ?
            of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/well+ordering"} well-ordered
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/set"} set
            whose
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cardinality"} cardinality
            is countable (i.e., either
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+set"} finite
            or
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+numbers"} denumerable
          %p
            Countable ordinals play an important role in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/recursion"} recursion
            theory,
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/computability+theory"} computability theory
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/proof+theory"} proof theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/consistency"} consistency
            strength of formal
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/theories"} theories
            via
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ordinal+analysis"} ordinal analysis
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/philosophy+of+mathematics"} philosophy of mathematics
            = succeed "\u201D." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/predicativity"} predicative
          %h2#definitions Definitions
          %p
            As indicated above, countable ordinals can be defined structurally as countable well-ordered sets (or “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/wosets"}> wosets
            ”). As is the case with any ordered set, a woset
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi W
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
            can be regarded as a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coalgebra+over+an+endofunctor"} coalgebra
            over the covariant
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/power-set"} power-set
            functor,
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi θ
                  %mo :
                  %mi W
                  %mo →
                  %mi P
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi W
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \theta: W \to P(W)
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \,
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %mo ↦
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mi y
                  %mo :
                  %mi y
                  %mo &lt;
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \mapsto \{y: y \lt x\}.
          %p
            A coalgebra map
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo :
                  %mi W
                  %mo →
                  %mi W
                  %mo ′
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f: W \to W'
            between wosets, aka a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simulation"} simulation
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            of countable wosets and simulations, thus ordered by inclusion, is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/preorder"} preorder
            and in fact equivalent to a woset. In
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/material+set+theory"} material set theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/first+uncountable+ordinal"} first uncountable ordinal
            (well-ordered set under the membership relation), often denoted
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi ω
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega_1
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/structural+set+theory"} Structurally
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi ω
                    %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega_1
            up to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
            as a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/skeleton"} skeleton
            of the category of countable ordinals, and so the study of countable ordinals becomes a study of the order structure of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi ω
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega_1
          %p
            This
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi ω
                    %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega_1
            has no top element (of course not: otherwise
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi ω
                    %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega_1
            would be a countable ordinal), and much of the interest and fun of the subject lies in playing the childhood game of seeing who can name the bigger number, or in this case the bigger countable ordinal. A key fact is that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi ω
                    %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega_1
            is countably cocomplete, and therefore behaves like a self-contained
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universe"} universe
            with respect to countably cocontinuous operations. There is quite a lot of scope in what one can build up to using such operations. After playing the larger ordinal game for a while, and becoming impressed by the sizes of ordinals one can define – while recognizing at the same time that one is “never getting anywhere” relative to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi ω
                    %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega_1
            itself – it is hard not to become awestruck by the staggering immensity of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi ω
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega_1
          %p
            Anyone who is unimpressed by the size of large countable ordinals has almost surely never seriously played with them. For that matter, people who are unimpressed by large
            %em finite
            numbers have probably never played around with them either, or at least not all that imaginatively! (And interestingly, one can use large countable ordinals reflectively to construct enormous integers, or one can use large
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/uncountable+ordinals"} uncountable ordinals
            reflectively to construct enormous countable ordinals.)
          %h2#fixed_points_and_the_veblen_hierarchy Fixed points and the Veblen hierarchy
          %p
            Here we discuss the use of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fixed+point"} fixed point
            theory in describing the lower stages of the Veblen hierarchies of countable ordinals, which will lead up to the Feferman-Schütte ordinal. We freely allow ourselves to reason classically and use the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principle+of+excluded+middle"} principle of excluded middle
          %p
            The ordinal
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi ω
                    %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega_1
            is countably
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cocomplete+category"} cocomplete
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo :
                  %msub
                    %mi ω
                    %mn 1
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mi ω
                    %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f: \omega_1 \to \omega_1
            that preserve
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimits"} colimits
            of countable (finite or denumerable) diagrams – or countable chains, without loss of generality. We’ll call such maps
            = succeed "," do
              %em continuous
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %mo ≤
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \leq f(x)
            for all
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo ∈
                    %msub
                      %mi ω
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in \omega_1
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            is
            = succeed "." do
              %em inflationary
          %p
            Preservation of colimits of finite nonempty chains comes for free, so we can ignore that. The colimit of the empty chain is the bottom element
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0
          %p
            The first result is a baby form of a general theorem due to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Adamek"} Adámek
            on
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/initial+algebras+of+endofunctors"} initial algebras of endofunctors
          #fix.num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              Suppose
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo :
                    %msub
                      %mi ω
                      %mn 1
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi ω
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f: \omega_1 \to \omega_1
              is inflationary and continuous. Then every
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo ∈
                    %msub
                      %mi ω
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in \omega_1
              has an upper bound that is a fixed point under
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
          .proof
            %h6#proof Proof
            %p
              For any
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo ′
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x'
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo ≤
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≤
                    %msup
                      %mi f
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≤
                    %mi …
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \leq f(x) \leq f^2(x) \leq \ldots
              exists, and since
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              preserves countable colimits,
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo ′
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x'
              is a fixed point of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
          .num_lemma
            %h6#lemma Lemma
            %p
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo :
                    %msub
                      %mi ω
                      %mn 1
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi ω
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f: \omega_1 \to \omega_1
              is order-preserving and satisfies
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi β
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi sup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi α
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                    %mi α
                    %mo &lt;
                    %mi β
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f(\beta) = \sup \{f(\alpha): \alpha \lt \beta\}
              for all limit (i.e., non-successor) ordinals
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi β
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \beta
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              is continuous.
          %p The converse of this result is trivially true.
          .proof
            %h6#proof_2 Proof
            %p
              For the case
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi β
                      %mo =
                      %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \beta = 0
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi α
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                    %mi α
                    %mo &lt;
                    %mi β
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{f(\alpha): \alpha \lt \beta\}
              is empty and thus has
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0
              as its supremum, so
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 0
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f(0) = 0
            %p
              Suppose that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi β
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \beta
              is the colimit of a chain
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi x
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ≤
                    %msub
                      %mi x
                      %mn 2
                    %mo ≤
                    %mi …
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x_1 \leq x_2 \leq \ldots
              with countably infinite image. Then this chain is
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cofinal+functor"} cofinal
              in the set
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %mi α
                      %mo :
                      %mi α
                      %mo &lt;
                      %mi β
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{\alpha: \alpha \lt \beta\}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi x
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≤
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi x
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≤
                    %mi …
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f(x_1) \leq f(x_2) \leq \ldots
              is cofinal in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi α
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo :
                      %mi α
                      %mo &lt;
                      %mi β
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{f(\alpha): \alpha \lt \beta\}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supremum"} supremum
              of
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi α
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo :
                      %mi α
                      %mo &lt;
                      %mi β
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{f(\alpha): \alpha \lt \beta\}
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi β
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f(\beta)
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_2 Proposition
            %p
              Suppose
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo :
                    %msub
                      %mi ω
                      %mn 1
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi ω
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f: \omega_1 \to \omega_1
              is inflationary and continuous. Define
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo ′
                    %mo :
                    %msub
                      %mi ω
                      %mn 1
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi ω
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f': \omega_1 \to \omega_1
              to be the function that takes each
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo ∈
                    %msub
                      %mi ω
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in \omega_1
              to the least fixed point of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              that is greater than
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo ′
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f'(y)
              for all
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi y
                      %mo &lt;
                      %mi x
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y \lt x
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo ′
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f'
              is also inflationary and continuous.
          .proof
            %h6#proof_3 Proof
            %p
              By definition,
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo ′
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo &lt;
                    %mi f
                    %mo ′
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f'(y) \lt f'(x)
              whenever
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi y
                      %mo &lt;
                      %mi x
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y \lt x
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo ′
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f'
              is order-preserving. That
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo ′
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f'
              is inflationary is proved by
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/induction"} induction
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi α
                    %mo ≤
                    %mi f
                    %mo ′
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi α
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha \leq f'(\alpha)
              for all
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi α
                      %mo &lt;
                      %mi β
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha \lt \beta
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi α
                    %mo ≤
                    %mi f
                    %mo ′
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi α
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo &lt;
                    %mi f
                    %mo ′
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi β
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha \leq f'(\alpha) \lt f'(\beta)
              i.e.
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi α
                    %mo &lt;
                    %mi f
                    %mo ′
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi β
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha \lt f'(\beta)
              for all
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi α
                      %mo &lt;
                      %mi β
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha \lt \beta
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi β
                      %mo ≤
                      %mi f
                      %mo ′
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi β
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \beta \leq f'(\beta)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo ′
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f'
              is continuous, let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi β
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \beta
              be a non-successor; by continuity of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              we have
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi sup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mi f
                    %mo ′
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi α
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                    %mi α
                    %mo &lt;
                    %mi β
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi sup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi f
                    %mo ′
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi α
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                    %mi α
                    %mo &lt;
                    %mi β
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mo =
                    %mi sup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mi f
                    %mo ′
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi α
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                    %mi α
                    %mo &lt;
                    %mi β
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f(\sup \{f'(\alpha): \alpha \lt \beta\}) = \sup \{f(f'(\alpha)): \alpha \lt \beta\} = \sup \{f'(\alpha): \alpha \lt \beta\}
            %p
              so that this supremum is in fact a fixed point of
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              greater than every
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo ′
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi α
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f'(\alpha)
              for
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi α
                      %mo &lt;
                      %mi β
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha \lt \beta
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo ′
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f'
              that
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo ′
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi β
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi sup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mi f
                    %mo ′
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi α
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                    %mi α
                    %mo &lt;
                    %mi β
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f'(\beta) = \sup \{f'(\alpha): \alpha \lt \beta\}
            %p
              and so, by the preceding lemma,
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo ′
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f'
              is continuous.
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition Definition
            %p
              The
              %em Veblen hierarchy
              is a family of functions
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi f
                        %mi α
                      %mo :
                      %msub
                        %mi ω
                        %mn 1
                      %mo →
                      %msub
                        %mi ω
                        %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_\alpha: \omega_1 \to \omega_1
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi α
                      %mo ∈
                      %msub
                        %mi ω
                        %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha \in \omega_1
            %ul
              %li
                Define
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi f
                        %mn 0
                      %mo :
                      %msub
                        %mi ω
                        %mn 1
                      %mo →
                      %msub
                        %mi ω
                        %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_0: \omega_1 \to \omega_1
                by
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi f
                          %mn 0
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi x
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo =
                        %mi sup
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                        %mi y
                        %mo +
                        %mn 2
                        %mo :
                        %mi y
                        %mo &lt;
                        %mi x
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_0(x) = \sup \{y+2: y \lt x\}
            %p This is inflationary, and continuous by the lemma.
            %ul
              %li
                Then define
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi f
                        %mi α
                      %mo :
                      %msub
                        %mi ω
                        %mn 1
                      %mo →
                      %msub
                        %mi ω
                        %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_\alpha: \omega_1 \to \omega_1
                by
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi f
                        %mrow
                          %mi α
                          %mo +
                          %mn 1
                      %mo =
                      %msubsup
                        %mi f
                        %mi α
                        %mo ′
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_{\alpha + 1} = f_\alpha^'
                and
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi f
                        %mi β
                      %mo =
                      %msub
                        %mi sup
                        %mrow
                          %mi α
                          %mo &lt;
                          %mi β
                      %msub
                        %mi f
                        %mi α
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_\beta = \sup_{\alpha \lt \beta} f_\alpha
                at limit ordinals
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi β
                        %mo &gt;
                        %mn 0
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \beta \gt 0
            %p
              By induction and the preceding proposition,
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mi α
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_\alpha
              is inflationary and continuous at successor cardinals
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi α
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi α
                    %mo &gt;
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha \gt 0
              since countable colimits of inflationary and continuous maps are also inflationary and continuous.
          %p
            It is worth contemplating the growth of the first few
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mi α
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_\alpha
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_0
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi f
                    %mn 0
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi α
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mi α
                  %mo +
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_0(\alpha) = \alpha + 1
            if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi α
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha
            is a successor, and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi f
                    %mn 0
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi α
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mi α
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_0(\alpha) = \alpha
            if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi α
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha
            is a limit ordinal.
          %p
            This means that next we have
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_1(0) = 0
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi ω
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_1(1) = \omega
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mn 2
                    %mi ω
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_1(2) = 2 \omega
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ω
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %msup
                      %mi ω
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_1(\omega) = \omega^2
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0
            is at
