              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi ϵ
                    %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \epsilon_0
            is sometimes considered the first reasonable thing to call a “large countable ordinal”. An
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ordinal+analysis"} ordinal analysis
            first carried by by Gerhard Gentzen asserts, roughly speaking, that the consistency of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peano+arithmetic"} Peano arithmetic
            is provable from
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/primitive+recursive+arithmetic"} primitive recursive arithmetic
            (which is weaker than PA) augmented by the principle of induction up to
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
